</head>
<body>

<div class="page">
    <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start;">
        <div>
            <h1 style="font-size: 36pt; margin-bottom: 10px;">iPrint Mobility Printing</h1>
            <p style="font-size: 16pt;">Android</p>
        </div>
        <div class="header-logo">
            <!-- Placeholder for University Logo -->
            <img src="placeholder_logo.png" alt="University Logo" style="height: 80px;">
            <div style="font-size: 14pt; text-align: right;">THE UNIVERSITY OF MEMPHIS</div>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div style="margin-top: 100px;">
        <p style="font-size: 12pt;">
            <span data-field="department_name">{{ department_name }}</span><br>
            <span data-field="address">{{ address }}</span><br>
            Phone: <span data-field="phone">{{ phone }}</span><br>
            Email: <span data-field="email">{{ email }}</span><br>
            <a href="#" style="color: blue;">umTech Website</a>
        </p>
    </div>
    <div style="position: absolute; bottom: 50px; left: 60px; font-size: 10pt; color: #555;">
        Revised: <span data-field="revision_date">{{ revision_date }}</span>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
    <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; margin-bottom: 30px;">
        <div style="font-size: 24pt;">THE UNIVERSITY OF MEMPHIS</div>
        <div class="footer">umTech | Page 1</div>
    </div>
    <h2 style="font-size: 20pt; margin-bottom: 20px;">Table of Contents</h2>
    <div style="margin-top: 20px;">
        <div class="toc-entry">
            <span>Connect to the UofM Wi-Fi Network ....................................................................</span>
            <span>3</span>
        </div>
        <div class="toc-entry">
            <span>Installing Mobility Print Printer Setup ...................................................................</span>
            <span>4</span>
        </div>
        <div class="toc-entry">
            <span>Printing on an Android.........................................................................................</span>
            <span>9</span>
        </div>
        <div class="toc-entry">
            <span>Locating Help Resources......................................................................................</span>
            <span>13</span>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
    <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; margin-bottom: 30px;">
        <div style="font-size: 24pt;">THE UNIVERSITY OF MEMPHIS</div>
        <div class="footer">umTech | Page 2</div>
    </div>
    <h2 style="font-size: 20pt; margin-bottom: 15px;">Purpose</h2>
    <p style="font-size: 12pt; margin-bottom: 20px;">
        This training material highlights how to install and use Papercut Mobility Printing on Android devices.
    </p>

    <h2 style="font-size: 20pt; margin-bottom: 15px;">Audience</h2>
    <p style="font-size: 12pt; margin-bottom: 30px;">
        This training material is designed for university faculty, staff, and students.
    </p>

    <h2 style="font-size: 20pt; margin-bottom: 15px;">Device Requirements</h2>
    <p style="font-size: 12pt;">
        Mobility Print supports Android <span data-field="min_os_version">{{ min_os_version }}</span>. Supported devices include Android phones and tablets from Google, Samsung, HTC, Lenovo, LG, Sony, and Huawei, among others.
    </p>
</div>

<div class="page">
    <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; margin-bottom: 30px;">
        <div style="font-size: 24pt;">THE UNIVERSITY OF MEMPHIS</div>
        <div class="footer">umTech | Page 3</div>
    </div>
    <h2 style="font-size: 20pt; margin-bottom: 15px;">Connect to the UofM Wi-Fi Network</h2>
    <p style="font-size: 12pt; margin-bottom: 20px;">
        For instructions on how to connect to the <span data-field="network_name">{{ network_name }}</span> Wi-Fi network, please see our <a href="#" style="color: blue;">umWireless documentation</a>.
    </p>
    <p style="font-size: 12pt;">
        <strong>Note:</strong> It is recommended that you connect to <span data-field="network_name">{{ network_name }}</span>, as these features are not available on <span data-field="guest_network">{{ guest_network }}</span>.
    </p>
</div>

<div class="page">
    <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; margin-bottom: 30px;">
        <div style="font-size: 24pt;">THE UNIVERSITY OF MEMPHIS</div>
        <div class="footer">umTech | Page 4</div>
    </div>
    <h2 style="font-size: 20pt; margin-bottom: 15px;">Installing Mobility Print Printer Setup</h2>
    <ol style="font-size: 12pt;">
        <li>
            If this is your first time using Mobility Print, you will need to install the <span data-field="app_name">{{ app_name }}</span> from the Google Play Store. You can download the app using this link or you can search for it directly in the Google Play Store.
        </li>
        <li>
            <p style="text-align: center; margin: 20px 0;">
                <!-- Placeholder for App Icon Image -->
                <img src="placeholder_icon.png" alt="Mobility Print Icon" style="width: 100px;">
            </p>
            <p style="text-align: center;">
                <span data-field="app_name">{{ app_name }}</span><br>
                <span data-field="version">{{ version }}</span><br>
                <span data-field="price">{{ price }}</span>
            </p>
        </li>
    </ol>
</div>

<div class="page">
    <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; margin-bottom: 30px;">
        <div style="font-size: 24pt;">THE UNIVERSITY OF MEMPHIS</div>
        <div class="footer">umTech | Page 5</div>
    </div>
    <ol style="font-size: 12pt;">
        <li>
            Next, <span data-field="app_name">{{ app_name }}</span> may ask for access to Photos/Media/Files, if so, click <strong>Accept</strong>.
        </li>
        <li>
            Google Play may ask you to complete account set up. Click <strong>Continue</strong>, to review your account and install apps on Google Play.
        </li>
        <li>
            You can choose to skip this step. By clicking <strong>Skip</strong>.
        </li>
        <li>
            <p style="text-align: center; margin: 20px 0;">
                <!-- Placeholder for Account Setup Image -->
                <img src="placeholder_account_setup.png" alt="Account Setup Screen" style="width: 100%;">
            </p>
            <p style="text-align: center;">
                Complete account setup<br>
                Review your account to continue installing apps on Google Play.
            </p>
        </li>
        <li>
            <p style="text-align: center; margin: 20px 0;">
                <!-- Placeholder for Payment Options Image -->
                <img src="placeholder_payment_options.png" alt="Payment Options Screen" style="width: 100%;">
            </p>
            <p style="text-align: center;">
                Add a payment option to complete your account. You won't be charged unless you make a purchase.
                <br>
                <span data-field="payment_method_1">{{ payment_method_1 }}</span>
                <br>
                <span data-field="payment_method_2">{{ payment_method_2 }}</span>
                <br>
                <span data-field="payment_method_3">{{ payment_method_3 }}</span>
            </p>
        </li>
    </ol>
</div>

<div class="page">
    <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; margin-bottom: 30px;">
        <div style="font-size: 24pt;">THE UNIVERSITY OF MEMPHIS</div>
        <div class="footer">umTech | Page 6</div>
    </div>
    <ol style="font-size: 12pt;">
        <li>
            The software will begin to install.
        </li>
        <li>
            <p style="text-align: center; margin: 20px 0;">
                <!-- Placeholder for Installation Screen -->
                <img src="placeholder_installing.png" alt="Installation Screen" style="width: 100%;">
            </p>
            <p style="text-align: center;">
                <span data-field="app_name">{{ app_name }}</span><br>
                Papercut Software
            </p>
        </li>
        <li>
            Tap <strong>Open</strong>.
        </li>
        <li>
            <p style="text-align: center; margin: 20px 0;">
                <!-- Placeholder for Open Screen -->
                <img src="placeholder_open.png" alt="Open App Screen" style="width: 100%;">
            </p>
            <p style="text-align: center;">
                <span data-field="app_name">{{ app_name }}</span><br>
                Papercut Software
            </p>
        </li>
    </ol>
</div>

<div class="page">
    <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; margin-bottom: 30px;">
        <div style="font-size: 24pt;">THE UNIVERSITY OF MEMPHIS</div>
        <div class="footer">umTech | Page 7</div>
    </div>
    <ol style="font-size: 12pt;">
        <li>
            Next, tap <strong>Android Settings</strong>.
        </li>
        <li>
            <p style="text-align: center; margin: 20px 0;">
                <!-- Placeholder for Settings Screen -->
                <img src="placeholder_settings.png" alt="Android Settings Screen" style="width: 100%;">
            </p>
            <p style="text-align: center;">
                <span data-field="app_name">{{ app_name }}</span>
            </p>
        </li>
        <li>
            Select the Mobility Print Settings Button to enable the service. Tap on the toggle button in the top-right corner of your screen to set it to <strong>ON</strong>.
        </li>
        <li>
            <p style="text-align: center; margin: 20px 0;">
                <!-- Placeholder for Toggle Screen -->
                <img src="placeholder_toggle.png" alt="Toggle Switch Screen" style="width: 100%;">
            </p>
            <p style="text-align: center;">
                <span data-field="app_name">{{ app_name }}</span>
            </p>
        </li>
    </ol>
</div>




<div class="page">
    <div style="text-align: left;">
        <div class="header-logo">THE UNIVERSITY OF MEMPHIS</div>
    </div>

    <div style="margin-top: 40px;">
        <div class="section-title">10.</div>
        <p>A list of available printers should appear once Mobility Print has been switched to the on position.</p>
        <div class="image-placeholder">Image Placeholder for Printer List</div>
        <div style="margin-top: 20px;">
            <p>11. Exit settings.</p>
            <p class="note">Note: If you want to use more than one printer on campus, repeat these steps for each printer.</p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="footer">umTech | Page 8</div>
</div>

<div class="page">
    <div style="text-align: left;">
        <div class="header-logo">THE UNIVERSITY OF MEMPHIS</div>
        <h1 style="font-size: 18pt; margin-top: 20px;">Printing on an Android</h1>
    </div>

    <div style="margin-top: 40px;">
        <p>1. To print, open the content you want to print.</p>
        <p class="note">Note: Printing may vary from program to program.</p>
        <div class="image-placeholder">Image Placeholder for Chrome App Menu</div>

        <p>2. In Chrome, open the app menu.</p>
        <div class="image-placeholder">Image Placeholder for Chrome Menu</div>

        <p>3. Tap Share.</p>
        <div class="image-placeholder">Image Placeholder for Share Menu</div>

        <p>4. Tap Print or the print icon to see a list of printers.</p>
        <div class="image-placeholder">Image Placeholder for Print Menu</div>

        <p>5. If you do not wish to use the default printer, tap the default printer and choose the correct one.</p>
        <div class="image-placeholder">Image Placeholder for Printer Selection</div>
        <p class="note">Note: Papercut printers have the Papercut logo beside them.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="footer">umTech | Page 9</div>
</div>

<div class="page">
    <div style="text-align: left;">
        <div class="header-logo">THE UNIVERSITY OF MEMPHIS</div>
        <h1 style="font-size: 18pt; margin-top: 20px;">Printing on an Android (Continued)</h1>
    </div>

    <div style="margin-top: 40px;">
        <p>6. To change the print settings, tap the down arrow in the center of the screen.</p>
        <div class="image-placeholder">Image Placeholder for Print Settings</div>

        <p>7. Once you have chosen your settings, tap Print.</p>
        <div class="image-placeholder">Image Placeholder for Final Print Settings</div>

        <p>8. A) Authenticate using your UofM credentials. B) Tap Print.</p>
        <div class="image-placeholder">Image Placeholder for Authentication Screen</div>
        <p class="note">Note: If you select the Remember me for 7 days checkbox, your tablet will remember your login details for that printer for one week.</p>

        <p>You may receive this message once your item has been sent to print. Click, OK.</p>
        <div class="image-placeholder">Image Placeholder for Mobility Print Confirmation</div>

        <p>9. Pick up your print from the specified printer.</p>
        <p class="note">Note: When printing multiple pages, keep your page amount below 50, or the print tab will reset.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="footer">umTech | Page 10</div>
</div>

<div class="page">
    <div style="text-align: left;">
        <div class="header-logo">THE UNIVERSITY OF MEMPHIS</div>
        <h1 style="font-size: 18pt; margin-top: 20px;">Locating Help Resources</h1>
    </div>

    <div style="margin-top: 40px;">
        <p>umTech offers technical support and resources to faculty, staff, and students. Assistance can be found through any of the support services below:</p>

        <p>Submitting a Service Request</p>
        <p>Login URL: Click here to access our service desk ticketing system. After logging in, choose the appropriate form to request services.</p>

        <p>Contact the ITS Service Desk</p>
        <p>ITS Service Desk – <span data-field="phone_number">{{ phone_number }}</span> any day of the week! (Excluding Some Holidays)</p>
        <p>ITS Service Desk Walk-In hours (Admin Building Room 100):</p>
        <ul>
            <li>Monday – Friday 8:00 am – 4:30 pm</li>
            <li>The ITS Service Desk Call Center hours:</li>
            <li>Monday – Friday 8:00 am – 8:00 pm</li>
            <li>Saturday 10:00 am – 2:00 pm</li>
            <li>Sunday 1:00 pm – 5:00 pm</li>
        </ul>

        <p>Contact the Service Desk for assistance with technical login problems or issues. Voicemail services will handle ALL incoming calls after hours. If you require assistance after 8:00 pm, please leave a message or <a href="#">submit a service request</a>.</p>

        <p>Voice messages will be relayed regularly and will receive a priority response the following business day. You may also email umTech at <span data-field="email_address">{{ email_address }}</span>. (Note: Using this email will automatically generate a service request.)</p>

        <p>Important Links</p>
        <p><a href="#">Explore the umTech Website</a></p>
        <p><a href="#">Search the Solutions Page</a></p>
    </div>

    <div class="footer">umTech | Page 13</div>
</div>

</body>
</html>